=== Atom: Pure Object-Oriented ===

In Atom, everything is an object.
Even strings respond to messages!

Examples:
  "text".println()   # String receives println message
  "text".print()     # String receives print message

This follows Smalltalk's philosophy:
  - Pure message passing
  - No global functions
  - Objects respond to messages

Just like 1 + 2 is really 1.add(2),
printing is message.println()!
